<http://data.silknow.org/object/25d88500-0d02-37aa-90d5-bc6e87c49849/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Made by sewing together 2 lengths of indigo coloured home-spun cloth, to form a central seam and then folding the fabric in half (the fold forming the shoulders). Holes are left in the upper corners for the arms and another opening is left in the centre seam for the neck.\nThe lower half of the garment is covered with bands of Job's Tears and yellow and red silk embroidery. Neckline and armholes are highlighted with red cloth and Job's Tears. (\"coix lacryma\" - seeds of a type of grass)."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/25d88500-0d02-37aa-90d5-bc6e87c49849> .

